// @exec: {"yield_time_ms": 30000, "max_output_tokens": 20000}
const replies = [
  ["PRRT_kwDOThd_Gc6UHXnA", "Agreed — addressed in 379c552. The plan now requires a Builder execution fee recipient in sidecar config and in the unsigned-bid request, threads it into the Engine payload attributes, and forbids falling back to the proposer/self-build fee-recipient cache. It now states explicitly that payload `feeRecipient` pays the Builder while `bid.fee_recipient` pays the proposer. The BN remains the Engine API owner, and the missing Beacon API/Lodestar work is now explicit."],
  ["PRRT_kwDOThd_Gc6UzBsh", "Updated in 379c552. The first loop no longer treats zero blobs as a payload choice: it accepts the payload the EL builds, and if blobs are present the BN must retain the KZG material, convert blobs to cells/columns, and disseminate the data-column sidecars. `DATA-01` still forces a non-zero-blob case for final core evidence."],
  ["PRRT_kwDOThd_Gc6U2fAs", "Agreed — the BN-owned Engine API and payload-building design is preserved. In 379c552, `D-04`, `API-02`, and `BN-01` now make closing the missing API surface and feeding implementation evidence upstream explicit, including the current Beacon API gaps tracked in #595 and #599."],
  ["PRRT_kwDOThd_Gc6U2jcp", "Updated in 379c552. The deterministic happy-path fixture now pins `--builder.selection=builderalways`, or alternatively `--builder.selection=maxprofit` with a documented boost factor. I also linked the Lodestar validator CLI reference and added this as an acceptance scenario."],
  ["PRRT_kwDOThd_Gc6U2mMU", "Updated in 379c552. Bid publication now has a bounded configurable offset from the first implementation, with immediate publication as the default. `BID-01` records candidate-ready/publication timestamps and includes timing-offset tests so Kurtosis can expose propagation issues as the spec changes."],
  ["PRRT_kwDOThd_Gc6U2n2G", "Added in 379c552. Proposer-equivocation validation stays BN-owned, and the core QA path now uses a bounded Deathstar Kurtosis fixture to prove the BN refuses envelope publication after proposer equivocation. The plan calls for adding the narrow BN validation if the pinned baseline still lacks it."],
  ["PRRT_kwDOThd_Gc6U2vtM", "Added as `EXT-OBS-01` in 379c552: a bounded stretch package for a small Lodestar Builder Grafana dashboard covering candidate outcomes, publication timing, selection, reveal, FULL/EMPTY outcomes, source-BN errors, and bounded status/balance visibility."],
  ["PRRT_kwDOThd_Gc6U2wpC", "Agreed. 379c552 now states that no Builder remote-signer contract is defined, keeps one local keystore-backed key in core, and defers remote signing/multiple keys until a supported specification exists. The internal signer boundary remains narrow for that future work."],
