I found a safe way to improve the GitHub mirror without rebuilding it:

- hide Linear Backlog items from the active workflow board, so 37 future items no longer masquerade as Todo;
- align PLAN-01 and CLI-01 with the existing In Review column;
- rename that view to “Active workflow”;
- leave the complete All issues and extension views unchanged.

GitHub requires the separate `project` write scope for those Project-only edits. I’m requesting that scope now. It affects only Projects you explicitly edit, creates no cost, and does not change repository or organization access.

